Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — individual review draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: Individual scene draft; whole-film pass provisionally accepted, individual author review pending

EXT./INT. COTTAGE/TRAILER/HUNTERS' VEHICLE - LATER

Reyes watches the cottage without entering. Vale traces an old ownership record, then inspects the place and photographs what is actually there. Voss follows the moving transmitter east and recovers it from the trailer.

At their regroup the positions do not add up to a current address. Vale notes evidence of a girl who watched and planned; Reyes calls it luck. Voss moves Zoe from passive passenger to active observer on their working map. None of them has located the farmhouse.
